      {
        "heading": "The short version",
        "text": "Cristian José Mena (born December 21, 2002) is a Dominican professional baseball pitcher for the Arizona Diamondbacks of Major League Baseball (MLB). He made his MLB debut in 2024."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Lately",
        "text": "Mena was optioned to Triple-A Reno to begin the 2025 season. He was recalled to the Diamondbacks on June 1, 2025. In three appearances for Arizona, Mena posted a 1–0 record and 1.35 ERA with eight strikeouts across 6+2⁄3 innings pitched. He was placed on the injured list on June 7, due to a teres major strain. Mena was transferred to the 60-day injured list on June 10. On March 25, 2026, Mena was placed on the 60-day injured list due to a right shoulder strain. On June 2, it was announced that Mena would undergo shoulder surgery, likely ending his season."
      }
    ],
